   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "**sich lassen** + infinitive",
     "texto": [
      "It is formed with conjugated **sich lassen** + infinitive at the end: **Das Problem lässt sich lösen** (the problem can be solved). The grammatical subject is the thing that can be done. In many contexts it is equivalent to **sein + zu + infinitive**, but the register and the nuance change."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "**sein + zu** + infinitive",
     "texto": [
      "It is a formal alternative to the passive with a modal. Depending on the context it expresses obligation (**Die Rechnung ist sofort zu bezahlen**: the invoice has to be paid immediately) or possibility (**Das Problem ist leicht zu lösen**: the problem can be solved easily). The verb keeps **zu** and goes at the end. It is not always equivalent to **sich lassen**: the first form appears a lot in instructions and formal texts."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Forms in the past",
     "texto": [
      "In the Präteritum: **Das ließ sich nicht vermeiden** (that could not be avoided). In the Perfekt: **Das hat sich nicht vermeiden lassen**. In this construction with two infinitives, **haben** is used."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
